course: dictionary
lesson: 13638
title: Inert: not moving, or not reacting
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word inert has three meanings: not moving, not reacting with other chemicals, and slow and not wanting to act. Read the words around it to decide.
explain: «The frog lay inert on the path and did not move at all.» The clues are lay and did not move at all, so inert means not moving and without life. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check that it still makes sense.
explain: In science, «Helium is an inert gas, so it does not easily react with other chemicals.» The words gas and the science topic are clues that inert means not reacting. This is why helium is safe to put in balloons.
fact: Inert means not moving, or without strength or life.
fact: In science, inert means not reacting with other chemicals.
fact: Inert gases such as helium, neon and argon do not easily react.
fact: Inert can also mean slow and not wanting to act.
fact: Helium is safe in balloons because it is an inert gas.
exercise: «He lay inert on the floor after he fell.» What does inert mean here? | Hungry and tired | Bouncing up and down | *Not moving and without life | Very loud and noisy
exercise: «Neon is an inert gas.» What does inert mean in science? | Glows brightly in the dark | *Does not easily react with other chemicals | Is very hot to touch | Always changes colour
exercise: «Sam felt inert after the long lunch and did not want to do anything.» What does inert suggest? | Full of energy and ready to run | Very cold | Angry and loud | *Slow and not wanting to act
test: «The inert balloon stayed on the shelf and did not move.» Which meaning fits best? | Red and shiny | Bright and loud | Floating high in the air | *Not moving
test: «Helium is inert, so it is safe to fill balloons with.» What does inert tell us about helium? | *It does not easily react with other chemicals | It is always moving | It is a liquid | It reacts quickly with everything
exam: «The old robot stood inert in the corner, its battery empty.» What does inert mean? | Dancing around the room | Hot and bubbly | Very bright and glowing | *Not moving or working
